**Loads**: controllers, filters, `@ControllerAdvice`, `WebMvcConfigurer`, Jackson configuration.

**Does not load**: services, repositories, security config, scheduled tasks — anything below the web layer.

**Test**: request/response mapping, status codes, validation, exception handling.

```java
@WebMvcTest(OrderController.class)
class OrderControllerTest {
    @Autowired private MockMvc mockMvc;
    @MockBean private OrderService orderService; // mock the dependency

    @Test
    void shouldReturnOrderById() throws Exception {
        given(orderService.findById(1L)).willReturn(mockOrder);

        mockMvc.perform(get("/api/orders/1"))
            .andExpect(status().isOk())
            .andExpect(jsonPath("$.status").value("DELIVERED"));
    }
}
```

**Not for**: business logic — use plain unit tests for that.

**Loads**: JPA repositories, entity classes, `EntityManager`, datasource config.

**Does not load**: services, controllers, security, the web layer.

Each test runs in a **transaction that rolls back** after completion, so tests stay isolated and clean.

```java
@DataJpaTest
class OrderRepositoryTest {
    @Autowired private OrderRepository orderRepository;
    @Autowired private TestEntityManager entityManager;
}
```

**Watch out**: it uses an **in-memory H2** database by default. If your app relies on database-specific behaviour (PostgreSQL JSONB, native functions, custom types), H2 will not catch the bug — pair it with **Testcontainers**:

```java
@DataJpaTest
@Testcontainers
@AutoConfigureTestDatabase(replace = NONE)
class OrderRepositoryTest { /* ... */ }
```

**Loads**: Jackson `ObjectMapper` and JSON components only.

**Does not load**: web layer, JPA, services, your application beans.

**Great for** verifying the serialization contract without booting the app:
- Date formats
- Property names
- Null handling
- Custom serializers and deserialization rules

```java
@JsonTest
class OrderDtoJsonTest {
    @Autowired private ObjectMapper objectMapper;

    @Test
    void shouldSerializeOrderDto() throws Exception {
        String json = objectMapper.writeValueAsString(dto);
        assertThat(json).contains("DELIVERED");
    }
}
```

It tests an **outbound HTTP client** without calling the real external service.

```java
@RestClientTest(PaymentGatewayClient.class)
class PaymentGatewayClientTest {
    @Autowired private PaymentGatewayClient client;
    @Autowired private MockRestServiceServer server;
}
```

**Verifies**:
- URL construction
- Headers
- Request serialization
- Response mapping
- Error handling

This keeps tests fast and deterministic — no network, no third-party downtime.

Load the security configuration and exercise it through `MockMvc`:

```java
@SpringBootTest
@AutoConfigureMockMvc
class SecurityConfigTest {
    @Autowired private MockMvc mockMvc;

    @Test
    void shouldRequireAuthForProtectedEndpoint() throws Exception {
        mockMvc.perform(get("/api/orders"))
            .andExpect(status().isUnauthorized());
    }
}
```

**Use for**: auth rules, roles/permissions, security filters.

Helpers like `@WithMockUser` set up an authenticated principal for role-based cases.

The **reactive** equivalent of `@WebMvcTest`.

**Loads**: `@Controller`/`@ControllerAdvice` and WebFlux config.
**Does not load**: services, JPA, other layers.

```java
@WebFluxTest(OrderHandler.class)
class OrderHandlerTest {
    @Autowired private WebTestClient webTestClient;

    @Test
    void shouldReturnOrder() {
        webTestClient.get().uri("/api/orders/1")
            .exchange()
            .expectStatus().isOk();
    }
}
```
